      "source": "https://roadsidethoughts.com/co/bond-xx-eagle-profile.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bond’s post office opened December 4, 1935, and the town became a stop for most passenger trains on the D&RGW main line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bond%2C_Colorado"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1932 the D&RGW began building the Dotsero Cutoff, and when finished in 1934 the line from Bond to Craig became a spur.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bond%2C_Colorado"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Bond’s elevation makes it one of the higher points along the Colorado River Headwaters Scenic Byway, a route celebrated for its rugged beauty.",
